unix: the main stack limit a variant may set

main() limits the C stack to a fixed 40000 bytes. A FLAT executable on noMMU Linux has the
stack elf2flt gives it at link time and nothing grows it, so a variant for one sets
MICROPY_UNIX_STACK_LIMIT below that.

diff --git a/ports/unix/main.c b/ports/unix/main.c
index 8f42d4f..50eafe2 100644
--- a/ports/unix/main.c
+++ b/ports/unix/main.c
@@ -441,7 +441,11 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
     #endif
 
     // Define a reasonable stack limit to detect stack overflow.
-    mp_uint_t stack_size = 40000 * UNIX_STACK_MULTIPLIER;
+    // A port variant may set its own (a fixed stack smaller than the default).
+    #ifndef MICROPY_UNIX_STACK_LIMIT
+    #define MICROPY_UNIX_STACK_LIMIT (40000)
+    #endif
+    mp_uint_t stack_size = MICROPY_UNIX_STACK_LIMIT * UNIX_STACK_MULTIPLIER;
 
     // We should capture stack top ASAP after start, and it should be
     // captured guaranteedly before any other stack variables are allocated.
